# Enemy_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Run-based or combat genres needing an enemy roster distinct from AI tech (roguelite).

## 2. This document owns
- Enemy design intent: role (pressure/punisher/support), threat tier, behavior summary, counter-play.
- Enemy rosters per phase/biome and combo/composition guidance.
- Elite/variant rules (what may modify a base enemy).

## 3. This document does NOT own
- AI implementation (perception/decision stacks) — AI_Systems.
- Numeric stats tables (when a separate balance doc exists) — Weapon_Balance-adjacent stat authority.
- Boss encounter staging — Encounter_Design.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Roster philosophy / 2. Roles & tiers / 3. Roster by phase / 4. Behavior intents / 5. Counter-play / 6. Elites & variants / 7. Composition guidance / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Enemy vs AI_Systems: *what an enemy wants* here; *how it computes* in AI_Systems.
- Behavior summaries reference AI archetypes by ID, not re-description.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every roster entry has a role and a counter-play line.
- Variant rules never create undeclared new behaviors.
